    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35135" root="قتب" body-key="q">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُتِّبَ كَاهِلُهُ</span></b> , said of a man, (assumed tropical:)  <i>He was,</i> or
<i>became, such as is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَجْنَأُ</span>. (JK. [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجُلٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُقَتَّبُ الكَاهِلِ</span>, below.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِى كَاهِلِ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الفَرَسِ تَقْتِيبٌ</span> i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَنَأٌ</span> (tropical:)  [app. meaning <i>In the
withers of the horse is a bending over the breast</i>].
(A.)

